Project Overview

In this lab, I learned how to use Windows Server Backup to protect important business files and recover them after accidental deletion.

This project demonstrates a common real-world IT Support task where an administrator performs backups and restores lost files when users accidentally delete important documents.

Lab Environment
	•	Windows Server 2022
	•	VMware Workstation
	•	Windows Server Backup Feature
	•	Secondary virtual disk (E:) used as the backup destination

Objectives
	•	Install Windows Server Backup
	•	Configure a backup destination
	•	Create a custom backup
	•	Backup a business folder
	•	Simulate accidental file deletion
	•	Restore deleted files from backup

Steps Performed

1. Installed Windows Server Backup

Installed the Windows Server Backup feature using Add Roles and Features in Server Manager.

2. Created Test Data

Created a folder named:

C:\LabBackup

Inside the folder I created sample business files:
	•	employees.txt
	•	Payroll.txt
	•	Policies.txt

Configured Backup Storage
	•	Added a secondary virtual disk
	•	Initialized and formatted it
	•	Assigned drive letter E:
	•	Used it as the backup destination

4. Performed a Custom Backup

Configured a Backup Once job.

Selected:
	•	Custom Backup
	•	Added only C:\LabBackup
	•	Selected E: as the backup destination

The backup completed successfully.

Simulated Data Loss

Deleted:
	•	employees.txt

This simulated a user accidentally deleting an important business file.

6. Restored the Deleted File

Opened Windows Server Backup

Selected:
	•	Recover
	•	This Server
	•	Files and Folders
	•	Original Location

Recovered the deleted file successfully.

Windows Server Backup restored the deleted file while preserving the existing files.

