⸻

Key Lessons Learned
	•	Backups are different from the Recycle Bin.
	•	Deleted files can still be recovered even after the Recycle Bin is emptied, provided a backup exists.
	•	Keeping backups on a separate disk protects data if the primary drive fails.
	•	Regular backups are essential for business continuity.

Outcome

Successfully backed up and restored business files using Windows Server Backup, demonstrating practical backup and disaster recovery skills used by IT Support and System Administrators.
